.TH PIDP1-TEST 1 "25 November 2026" "pidp1-mods" "PiDP-1 User Commands"
.SH NAME
pidp1-test \- exercise the PiDP-1 hardware front panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pidp1-test
.br
.BI pidp1_test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pidp1-test
drives the PiDP-1 hardware front panel by hand, so dead lamps and stuck
switches can be found without a simulator running. It stops the running
simulation, starts the panel driver, runs the tests in
.B pidp1_test
and stops the driver again. The tests walk a light across the panel lamps,
print the switch and joystick state in octal for you to check against the
physical switches, and prompt you through each check.
.PP
.B pidp1_test
is the test program itself. Run it directly only while a panel driver is
already up (started by
.BR pdp1-test ,
the
.BR pdp1-panel
service, or
.BR pdp1control ),
as it only reads and writes the panel lines.
.PP
On a packaged install the panel's GPIO nodes belong to the
.B pidp1
group (the shipped udev rule), so a member of that group starts the panel
driver without a password; anyone else pays a
.BR sudo .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /var/lib/pidp1-mods
the state directory the simulation is started from
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR pdp1 (1),
.BR pdp1control (1)
